    "evidence_text": " Special operations are usually implemented through specific, tailored intelligence.\n\nBen Johnston (composer)\n\nPascale Criton\n\nPascale Criton (born 1954) is a French musicologist and a composer of contemporary music, more specifically microtonal music.\n\nHuygens-Fokker Foundation\n\n The Foundation presents frequent concerts (originally in Teylers Museum) presenting contemporary, early, popular, and improvised microtonal music.\n\n The current director is Sander Germanus.\n\nMarcus Warren Hobbs\n\nElaine Walker (composer)\n\nElaine Walker is a composer, electronic musician, and theorist.\n\n She specializes in microtonal music, including founding ZIA, an all electronic band, and performing with D.D.T.\n\nBob Gilmore\n\n He studied music at York University, England, and Queen's University, Belfast (PhD.\n\n His biography of French-Canadian composer Claude Vivier was published by University of Rochester Press in June 2014.\n\nKnocking Piece II\n\nKnocking Piece II is a piece of music by Ben Johnston.\n\n In both pieces, Johnston calls to demonstrate unconventional methods of playing conventional instruments.\n\nList of compositions by Alois H\u00e1ba\n\nNewband\n\nNewband is a contemporary music ensemble devoted to the performance of microtonal music.",
